{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented `OrderService.refund_order` and `OrderService.export_credit_note`. Each refund records a negative ledger entry and reverses the difference between cumulative tax due back and tax already refunded. This preserves the original subtotal and tax exactly, including across one-cent refunds. Credit notes export the recorded refund amounts as positive magnitudes.\n\nRefunds and upgrades share the ledger’s idempotency keys. Identical retries return the original entry. Conflicting retries, invalid inputs, and over-refunds raise `ValidationError` without recording another entry.\n\nAdded five refund tests. `run_checks.py` passed all 20 tests and exited 0."}}
